#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
"""A local web agent decided by Laya: a plan, deterministic rules, and narrow typed questions. Run: ./tools/laya-agent --demo

The laya-mlx sibling of SemIf's semif-agent (same shell: Playwright, indexed
element table, independent DONE verification, anti-loop machinery, traces),
with a Laya-native decision layer in the laya-ultrafast style:

1. ONE replaceable LLM command (--llm, default 'opencode run -m
   openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3'; swap for 'ollama run <model>' via LLM_COMMAND
   when you want everything local) serves every text part: it refines the
   raw goal once (concrete dates, explicit defaults, finish sentence),
   plans ONCE per task (the values the goal states, the item to open, the
   finish condition), and writes the final report.
2. Deterministic site-generic rules drive the loop: fill each stated value,
   submit, open the named item, wait for results.
3. Laya answers only the narrow questions it is good at, all in one predict
   call per cycle: which page kind is this (contrastive finish gate), which
   field receives a value (value-first), which button submits, which element
   opens the item. Zero output tokens in the decision path.

DONE is never trusted: the outcome is verified independently (--verify-text)
before success.

--model selects the Laya checkpoint (default aac6fef/laya-mlx, 512-token
context; aac6fef/laya-typed-decisions-mlx has 1024 and doubles the state
budget). --no-refine skips the refinement step (planning still runs).

Also try any page:  ./tools/laya-agent --url URL --goal '...' --verify-text '...'

Exit codes: 0 = done and verified, 1 = done but unverified, 2 = blocked/stalled,
3 = error.
"""

